1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,840
We'd like to introduce you to the first release of the native HTTP logger coming soon to BurpSuite.

2
00:00:10,840 --> 00:00:12,400
Let's head over to the Logger tab.

3
00:00:13,540 --> 00:00:19,120
Here we can see a list of log items with the request response viewer showing on selection.

4
00:00:19,940 --> 00:00:22,480
At the top we can see the capture filter summary.

5
00:00:22,960 --> 00:00:25,900
This provides a brief overview of what the logger is capturing.

6
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:29,920
You can see in the summary that the log limit is set to 50 megabytes.

7
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:32,000
Let's change this by clicking it.

8
00:00:33,280 --> 00:00:35,200
Here we're able to adjust the capture limit.

9
00:00:35,840 --> 00:00:39,040
We can make a selection from the drop down or enter a custom value.

10
00:00:39,920 --> 00:00:44,560
We advise limiting the amount of memory used by the logger so that performance isn't compromised.

11
00:00:45,520 --> 00:00:48,320
Let's set this to 100 megabytes and click apply.

12
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:56,160
Below the capture filter we can also change the view filters which will refine the data shown in the table below.

13
00:00:57,120 --> 00:01:05,280
Over to the right we can also configure the columns that are shown in the table and we can clear the log by clicking the trash icon.

14
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:09,760
We can also toggle the logger on and off by clicking the button here.

15
00:01:10,880 --> 00:01:12,880
So that's a simple overview of the logger tool.

16
00:01:12,880 --> 00:01:18,560
This will be available in the early adopter channel for both community and professional versions coming soon.

17
00:01:18,560 --> 00:01:20,560
We'll see you next time.

